## MQ Context Provider — Required Endpoints (Layer 3)

The MQ Context Provider service must expose these REST endpoints:

| Method | Path | Query Parameters |
|---|---|---|
| `GET` | `/health` | — |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/mq/queue-managers` | `region` (optional) |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/mq/queues` | `queue_manager`, `queue`, `time_range` |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/mq/channels` | `queue_manager`, `channel` |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/mq/alerts` | `queue_manager`, `severity`, `time_range`, `limit` |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/mq/dlq` | `queue_manager` |

Implement these routes in `mq-context-provider` following the same pattern as `servers-context-provider/alerts.py`, using `ObserveServerOperations.from_env()` from the `observability-common` library.

## Error Handling

| Error | Cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `Cannot reach MQ Context Provider` | Wrong URL or service not running | Check `MQ_CONTEXT_PROVIDER_URL` and that the service is up |
| `503 Service Unavailable` | MQ Context Provider cannot reach Observe | Check `OBSERVABILITY_MCP_URL` and `OBSERVABILITY_MCP_TOKEN` in the context provider |
| `401 Unauthorized` | Invalid token | Check `OBSERVABILITY_MCP_TOKEN` in the context provider |

## Layer Responsibilities

| Layer | Component | Knows about |
|---|---|---|
| 2 | `mqmcpserver_observe.py` | `MQ_CONTEXT_PROVIDER_URL` only |
| 3 | `mq-context-provider` | `OBSERVABILITY_MCP_URL`, `OBSERVABILITY_MCP_TOKEN` |
| 4 | `observability-common` | Observe MCP protocol and tool names |
